  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Justice and Peace Actors as catalysts of change</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 18-month project supports the the diocese of Marsabit, Kenya, in its 3-year implementation of a governance and advocacy project,  using Geo Information Systems (GIS) to produce real-time Geo maps of the conflict corridors and health sector facilities within Marsabit county.  

The project has formed and trained 16 Community Education and Leadership teams (CELTs) as a community resource group to provide information and facilitate engagement as public expenditure monitors and agents of peace.  These groups monitor service delivery in the water, education, health and security sector. A county liaison desk  links the community and the county assembly on policy and legislative matters. The project will:
- familiarise stakeholders with the concept of digital mapping;
- identify and train CELT members in GIS and manual data collection;
- conduct digital and manual data collection through the trained CELT members;
- analyse the data, and share it with local communities and county government to action;
- document and share case studies with other partners. 

The project output will then be used as a tool for CELTs, communities and other actors to seek action from the county government, particularly the departments of security and health.</narrative>
  </description>
